  "worked_solution": "When we divide the two functions, we get a constant, and the limit of a constant is just the constant itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{p(x)}{q(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3{x}^{3}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
